Z||000000||Loki||08-18-2001||05:13 PM||||OK last sunday I got my a/c fixed and found out my exhaust leak is worse than I thought it was. Anywho, since then the car idles very high, like 3k (foot off gas I go about 35-40  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) also its acting wierd. Can push on the gas but nothing happens for like 1-2 seconds, then wam im gone. Any clue? Oh, 86SE Auto V6<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||4
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-18-2001||05:20 PM||||Idles at 3000??? Sounds like your EGR tube is cracked.  Either that or your Idle air is stuck open.<P>Joe||||reg||5
Z||000002||Loki||08-18-2001||08:07 PM||||OK, checking EGR valve right now. where should the diaphram sit at idle? Ill the way out or in some?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||08-19-2001||03:32 AM||||You should be able to squeeze the diaphram up and it should go down by itself.  Check for binding, etc.<P>More than that, I think your car is sucking fresh air in....check that tube that goes from the EGR to the intake.  Take it off carfully...betch'ya find a crack in it.<P>Also, pull out the IAC and clean it, you'll want to check for a wobbly pintle.<P>These are the only things that I know that'll cause an engine to run that fast!<P>Of course you could have a big hole in something else(vac line, gasket)  Sounds silly, but is the throttle plate closed all the way?<P>Dunno without hearing it.  Still at a loss?  spray every gasket, vac line, hose with Carb cleaner and see if you see smoke/engine running different.<P>Good luck!<P><BR>||||reg||10
